		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4720&amp;p=34962#p34962"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>If by backup you're referring to backing up the radio's factory flash settings, you can't do that until after you've upgraded the radio to OpenGD77 firmware.<br><br>At that point, you then need to store the resulting backup file in two or more safe places in case you ever want to revert to the factory firmware.<br><br>I didn't try to backup my radio until after installing OpenGD77 (as detailed in the upgrade instructions), but I'm pretty sure you won't see a COM port in the OpenGD77 CPS until the radio has been ungraded. Edit: I see you've already answered that question for yourself.<br><br>Mike, ZL2MGS.</div></blockquote>That's what I don't understand "you can't do that until after you've upgraded the radio to OpenGD77 firmware".  I accidentally found that out.....as you mentioned...<br><br>MY QUESTION is that after installing OpenGD77, then the backup is not the original calibration, flash...etc OR am I missing something?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7427">kd4hoy</a> — Tue Dec 31, 2024 12:23 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
