		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4720&amp;p=34958#p34958"><![CDATA[
You can backup the original config first via the factory CPS, but this config can only be used with factory CPS.<br><br>The other backup is to backup the flash memory which contains data structures and config data for the factory firmware, this<br>backup is made as the first step after you have loaded OpenGD77 firmware but before you loaded any new config into the radio.<br><br>Normally the newly loaded OpenGD77 radio displays gibberish channel data in this step.<br><br>Radio should be powered on in normal mode (running OpenGD77) and then you go into Extras-&gt;OpenGD77 Support and click on "Backup Flash"<br><br>When you have saved the "Backup Flash" you can load a new codeplug from OpenGD77 which clears away the "gibberish"<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Mon Dec 30, 2024 9:50 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
