<blockquote class="uncited"><div>'ve reinstalled the CPS for the 390 and it installs without errors (even in event log) but there is no COM port</div></blockquote>It'ts not clear what CPS you are taking about or what "event log" you are referring to.<br><br>If you are referring to the official TYT CPS for this radio, then the only thing you can backup is the calibration data, and you normally access this my holding Control-T in the official CPS<br><br>You can of course also read the official codeplug in the radio using the official CPS.<br><br>If you want to use your existing codeplug, the only way you can do this is if you can export the channels etc to CSV files using the official CPS, assuming it supports exporting to CSV. But AFIK there is no tool to directly convert from the official CPS CSV files to the OpenGD77CPS exported CSV format.<br><br><br>and like ZL2MGS  says, the official CPS does not use a COM port.  You will only see a COM port after installing the OpenGD77 firmware, and this COM port won't work with the official CPS, as it doesn't use that method.<br><br>Also. You can only install the OpenGD77 firmware using the OpenGD77CPS PC exe or the linux python script.<br><br>And.. The OpenGD77 firmware must be running for the OpenGD77CPS to communicate with the radio, i.e the radio must NOT be in DFU mode.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Dec 30, 2024 9:46 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
