		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: TYT MD-UV390 GPS and NO COM Port]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4720&amp;p=34956#p34956"><![CDATA[
If by backup you're referring to backing up the radio's factory flash settings, you can't do that until after you've upgraded the radio to OpenGD77 firmware.<br><br>At that point, you then need to store the resulting backup file in two or more safe places in case you ever want to revert to the factory firmware.<br><br>I didn't try to backup my radio until after installing OpenGD77 (as detailed in the upgrade instructions), but I'm pretty sure you won't see a COM port in the OpenGD77 CPS until the radio has been ungraded. Edit: I see you've already answered that question for yourself.<br><br>Mike, ZL2MGS.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4176">ZL2MGS</a> — Mon Dec 30, 2024 9:26 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
